            <p>One of the more famous cruise ports in the Dominican Republic is Amber Cove! This new port on the north coast close to Puerto Plata has come a long way and now hosts ships from most of the major cruise lines, including <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/carnival-cruise-line.aspx">Carnival</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/royal-caribbean-cruises.aspx">Royal Caribbean</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/msc-cruise-line.aspx">MSC Cruises</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/norwegian-cruise-line.aspx">Norwegian Cruise Line</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/holland-america-cruises.aspx">Holland America Line</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/princess-cruises.aspx">Princess Cruises</a>, and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/celebrity-cruise-line.aspx">Celebrity Cruises</a>. In the port area, there are shops and restaurants surrounding a large pool complex that provides a friendly first impression. </p>
            <p>Amber Cove, Dominican Republic, is also a gateway to inland excitement and serene island rhythms. Guests can hike to waterfalls, take cable cars up nearby mountains, or wander through the historic colonial streets. Its visitor-friendly configuration enables guests to simply step off the ship and walk between it and the island activities of interest, thus allowing them more time to experience. </p>

